  "body": "## What changed\n\n#633: the field stock engine was about 300× slower than the column engine on a large box (found in PR #625's review). This blocked #589, the column engine's retirement.\n\n**Profile** (release, `drill_plate.cl` on a 120 mm box at the CLI's 0.375 mm auto cell, 320 × 320):\n\n| Phase | Column | Field, before | **Field, after** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Build the block | 27 µs | **58 s** | **42 µs** |\n| Cut (9 moves) | 23 µs | 3.4 ms | 2.6 ms |\n| Read every column | 0.2 ms | 66 ms | 53 ms |\n| Cut cells | 399 | 399 | **399** |\n\n- **Cause:** it was not the cutting (the M7.3 per-brick law, #584, holds). `block_field` meshes the floorless block **ten spans deep**, and `SdfField::from_mesh`'s BFS band-filled every cell along those 1.2 m walls.\n- **Fix:** a new `field_box::AnalyticBox`, the closed-form signed distance of an axis-aligned box.\n  - `SdfField::from_box` builds the block's shell, which is a handful of facets and still answers parity and bounds, and **stores no bricks**.\n  - `mag_at`, the single reader of the mesh layer, answers unstored cells from the box, clamped to `cap` by the existing band law.\n  - The cut layers and every other reader are unchanged. Cylinder and model stocks still band-fill, bounded by their real size.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/633-field-block-closed-form.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **New `crates/sim/tests/field_block_cost.rs`, 3/3:**\n  - `a_block_stores_no_band_at_build`: the 58 s case stores 0 bricks.\n  - `the_closed_form_reads_the_stock_the_band_fill_read`: across a lattice around a block, same sign everywhere and agreement within 2 cells with the band-filled field.\n  - `a_large_field_block_runs_a_drill_program_quickly`: heavy lane, release, a 120 mm block plus 4 plunges under 2 s.\n- **Heavy release lanes**, run to confirm verdicts are unchanged:\n  - `stock_engine_agreement`: 3/3, **0 findings**, every `max |delta|` 0.\n  - `stock_backend_parity`: 13/13.\n  - `stock_field_cost`: total **7.6 s (was 83.9 s)**. Build is 0.00 s on every golden program, at 0.19-10.9 ms/move.\n- **`scripts/gate.sh quick`:** the sim suites pass. Named: stock_columns 3, stock_preview 10, stock_bull_nose 7, wall_slack 5, headless_bin 3, and app stock_sim_document 9, stock_view 4, stock_play 7, setup_carry 9, carried_verify 8.\n- **Clippy** on sim and app with `-D warnings`: clean. No golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nCylinder and model-stock build cost. Those still band-fill; a closed-form cylinder can follow if profiling shows a need.\n\nChangelog: The field stock engine builds a block stock in microseconds instead of up to a minute (closed-form box distance) (#633)\n\nFixes #633\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
